==================================================================
   SKY130 ANALOG PARASITIC EXTRACTION (PEX) COMPREHENSIVE REPORT   
   Milestone: v1.4.0 — Physical Timing Correlation & Verification 
==================================================================
Extraction Tool        : Magic 8.3 (ext2spice cthresh 0.001)
Extraction Settings    : extract all; ext2spice cthresh 0.001; ext2spice format ngspice
Simulation Tool        : ngspice-42 batch post-layout transient execution

------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Layout Extraction Nodal & Parasitic Breakdown
------------------------------------------------------------------
Cell 1: pmos_pass_2000u.mag (64-Finger PMOS Pass Transistor)
  - Layout Geometry      : 64 fingers, W/L = 31.25 um / 0.15 um (Total W = 2000 um)
  - Number of Nets       : 67 extracted nets
    * 3 Primary Ports    : VDD_IN (Source), VREG (Drain), V_GATE (Gate)
    * 1 Substrate Well   : VDD_IN_WELL (N-well bulk tap)
    * 63 Finger Sub-nets : Distributed inter-finger diffusion & metal1/metal2 routing
  - Extracted Capacitors : 906 lumped nodal capacitors
  - Total Capacitance    : 1405.83 fF (1.406 pF)
    * Ground Capacitance : 1220.50 fF (86.8% — gate-oxide & diffusion-to-well)
    * Coupling Cap       : 185.33 fF (13.2% — gate-to-drain overlap & inter-finger metal)
  - Extracted Resistance : Lumped series metal drop included (R_on = 0.22 Ohm)

Cell 2: dac_5bit_array.mag (5-Bit Common-Centroid Resistor Ladder)
  - Layout Geometry      : 32 unit poly resistors (W = 1.0 um, L = 5.0 um), 8x4 common-centroid
  - Number of Nets       : 35 extracted nets (33 ladder taps + 2 perimeter dummy guard rings)
  - Extracted Capacitors : 415 inter-tap and nodal capacitors
  - Total Capacitance    : 32.01 fF
    * Ground Capacitance : 27.40 fF (85.6% — poly-to-substrate field oxide)
    * Inter-tap Coupling : 4.61 fF (14.4% — adjacent resistor line coupling)

------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Pre-Layout vs. Post-Layout (PEX) Electrical Performance Comparison
------------------------------------------------------------------
Test Setup: Closed-loop LDO regulator with folded-cascode error amplifier driving
extracted PMOS pass device. Load current step: 5 mA -> 50 mA (t_rise = 1.0 ns).

Performance Metric             | Pre-Layout     | Post-Layout (PEX)  | Delta / Impact
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DC Open-Loop Gain (dB)         | 68.4 dB        | 68.1 dB            | -0.3 dB (Metal drop)
Phase Margin (degrees)         | 74.92 deg      | 73.85 deg          | -1.07 deg (Parasitic C)
Unity Gain Bandwidth (MHz)     | 11.62 MHz      | 11.45 MHz          | -170 kHz
Peak Load Transient Droop (mV) | 42.1 mV        | 48.2 mV            | +6.1 mV droop
Settling Time to 1% (ns)       | 18.2 ns        | 26.6 ns            | +8.4 ns (+46.15%)
Quiescent Current (uA)         | 24.8 uA        | 24.8 uA            | 0.0 uA
Output Voltage Offset (mV)     | 1.8 mV         | 2.4 mV             | +0.6 mV
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PEX AUDIT DECLARATION:
1. Parasitic networks extracted natively from Magic layout databases using 1 aF threshold.
2. Transistor models used for simulation are simplified Level-1 SPICE models for
   architectural characterization; foundry BSIM4 models required for sign-off.
3. Settling time increase (+8.4 ns) is physically caused by the 1.406 pF gate-to-drain
   Miller capacitance and load-node parasitic capacitance slowing the loop slew-rate.
